      "content": "Even if your history suggests this is a migraine, the combination of one-sided vision changes and arm weakness requires immediate medical evaluation to rule out a stroke, especially since symptoms like weakness can occur in migraines but also in emergencies. Taking over-the-counter medication like sumatriptan while waiting could mask symptoms or interact dangerously with other conditions without a doctor's assessment. Please override your fear of the ER and call emergency services immediately; it is far better to be assured there is a problem than to lose time treating a potential stroke.",
